WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:04.910
Speaker 1: . You know, one of the things I've
said before and that I continue to say many

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:10.260
things I continue to say one is we can have
political disagreements with our leaders as

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:18.240
we will inevitably have while recognizing
that some leaders are normal and others are

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.380
not.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:26.310
And Joe Biden, despite not doing nearly everything
I want him to do, has brought back a degree

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:32.200
of respect to the United States globally that
Donald Trump only ever dreamed of.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:40.539
And this has become so clear during the recent
G7 and NATO summit and Joe Biden's various

00:00:40.539 --> 00:00:42.729
meetings with world leaders.

00:00:42.729 --> 00:00:49.749
Remember that under Donald Trump, world leaders
were regularly visibly annoyed with Trump,

00:00:49.749 --> 00:00:52.159
endlessly frustrated with Trump.

00:00:52.159 --> 00:00:57.499
Trump was increasingly just not a part of
important conversations that world leaders

00:00:57.499 --> 00:00:58.620
were having.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:05.720
The reporting from the G7 and NATO is stunning
how quickly respect has been restored to the

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.720
office.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.859
Now, that doesn't mean Biden's a hero.

00:01:07.859 --> 00:01:15.340
I've said so many times, let's not DFI politicians,
they're just people and they're flawed people.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.810
They're really just like you and me.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.030
It doesn't mean Biden is a hero.

00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:25.450
It's just a reminder of how disastrous the
four years under Donald Trump were.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:31.300
Now, first of all, statistically, before we
get to the sort of anecdotal stuff, Pew Research

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:36.700
Center released a report last week documenting
the huge improvement to the United States

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:43.649
stature globally after the inauguration of
Joe Biden and the portion of world citizens

00:01:43.649 --> 00:01:49.460
from 12 different countries with confidence
in the United States in the US president went

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:54.990
from 17 percent when Trump left office now
to 75 percent.

00:01:54.990 --> 00:01:56.679
These are just stunning numbers.

00:01:56.679 --> 00:02:03.740
This is basically a quadrupling of the confidence
in the American president in these early months

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.289
of Joe Biden's presidency compared to when
Donald Trump left office.

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:13.580
The portion of citizens in these 12 countries
with a favorable view of the United States

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:17.920
has nearly doubled, from 34 percent to 62
percent already.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.080
So statistically, when people like, you know,
free people from the my pillow rally say the

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:28.120
U.S. is now O'Shay, you know, the we should
be ashamed now.

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:29.470
The U.S. is embarrassed globally.

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.680
No, no, no, no, no.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:34.690
We have the data Pew Research Center studies
these this Noam Chomsky referred to it a couple

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:36.480
of weeks ago when we interviewed him.

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:40.739
The favorable view of the US has nearly doubled
around the world under Trump.

00:02:40.739 --> 00:02:46.140
But then anecdotally from the G7 and NATO,
Politico describes it as, quote, Overall,

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:51.080
the G7 has delivered a significant win for
Biden while the leaders were panned for not

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:56.680
doing enough to vaccinate the world and frequently
fell short of consensus on the toughest issues.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.920
They're definitely moving in the same direction.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:03.780
And other leaders fell over themselves to
welcome Biden to their table.

00:03:03.780 --> 00:03:09.540
When French President Macron was asked about
whether the US is back as a global leader,

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.810
Macron said definitely and later said, It's
great to have a US president, part of the

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.689
club and very willing to cooperate.

00:03:17.689 --> 00:03:22.730
German Chancellor Angela Merkel said to reporters
at the summit, quote, Being able to meet Joe

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:27.910
Biden is obviously important because he stands
for the commitment to multilateralism, which

00:03:27.910 --> 00:03:29.230
we were missing in recent years.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.599
That's a direct shot at Trump.

00:03:31.599 --> 00:03:35.760
Even British Prime Minister Boris Johnson,
who quite frankly, politically is an adversary

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:37.620
of Biden as a right winger.

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:42.579
Boris Johnson said he was, quote, absolutely
thrilled to see Biden and that speaking to

00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:45.829
Biden was, quote, a breath of fresh air.

00:03:45.829 --> 00:03:50.569
Heather Conley, who served as a deputy assistant
secretary of state to Bush-Cheney administration,

00:03:50.569 --> 00:03:53.030
said to Politico, quote, There is no longer
a.

00:03:53.030 --> 00:03:58.730
Feeling of complete, complete dread before
a NATO or G7 summit or fearing that the meetings

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:04.049
would upend U.S. policy, a Washington Post
report added, Biden was greeted with delight

00:04:04.049 --> 00:04:08.810
by G7 leaders, relieved that Trump's tantrums
will be replaced by Biden's backslapping.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.520
So let me say it again.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.510
We do not worship politicians on this show.

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:18.880
Biden is a very flawed politician and at the
end of the day, he's just a person.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:21.990
But to deny the clear difference here is to
ignore reality.

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:28.160
Now, obviously, and predictably, people on
the right are saying we now are globally embarrassed.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.580
That's not backed up by the data.

00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:34.580
But what is really sad is to see even people
on the left who see Biden not just as not

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.510
progressive enough, but who want to go further
and they want to pretend that we don't have

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:42.760
a night and day difference from what we had
under Trump guys.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:45.110
It's OK to recognize.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:48.420
And still to say, Biden hasn't done enough.

00:04:48.420 --> 00:04:50.300
Biden's not progressive enough.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.240
Biden may not achieve the things we want them.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.630
That's fine.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:05:01.930
It's OK to say Trump was a reality TV freak
show and Biden is a respectful, educated diplomat.

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.970
And that's a really good thing.

00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:06.750
But we still hold Biden accountable on policy.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.640
It's OK to do that.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:15.370
But the leftists who react to this by saying,
of course, Merkel and Boris Johnson, like

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:22.780
Biden, they're all the same center right,
neo liberal or whatever.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:27.900
Biden's policy platform is not that of Merkel.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.870
It is not that of Johnson.

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.940
Will he achieve everything he said he was
going to?

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:32.940
No, of course not.

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.930
And we'll hold him accountable when be critical.

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:40.170
But we really participate in a sort of collective
gaslighting.

00:05:40.170 --> 00:05:42.290
If we and by we I mean others.

00:05:42.290 --> 00:05:43.290
I'm not doing this.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:49.930
If we pretend that there's no night and day
difference between what Trump was and what

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:54.960
President Biden is today, you know, the thing
Trump could never buy, no matter how much

00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:01.140
he spent, no matter how much money he had
with class and professionalism and maturity

00:06:01.140 --> 00:06:04.500
and tact and diplomacy.

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:11.800
And that doesn't make Biden a progressive
hero by its very by merely being that way.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:15.241
But it changes dramatically the standing of
the United States around the world.

00:06:15.241 --> 00:06:15.253
And that's a really important thing.

